mapledmaaddr (#528) -- KILL TABLE 1, PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go in a
SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out) -- an append rewrites this file's mtime, which is the order evidence.

INSTRUMENT: regress/maple_dmaaddr_probe.py, frozen at launch as maple_dmaaddr_probe.FROZEN.py (16 rows; measured 16/16
on the fixed build/ binary before this block was written).  BASELINE: SEC dev_dreamcast_maple.c (the fix).  HEAD:
dev_dreamcast_maple.HEAD.c (`git show HEAD:').  MUTATOR: mut_maple.py (each find-text must occur exactly once).

ROW LIST, by Fable's pass-1 ruling (fable_pass1_20260912.md):
  FLOOR   read val_a, read val_b (the accept cell: POISONED destination, high + low-five bits); other read (RESET2 == 0,
          the dominating-predicate complement); marker survive + exit status (the exit(1) half); read silent (ANY maple
          text in the nine read sessions -- the channel, never one literal string)
  L1 (e)  initial zero, read four, read all ones, double read 1/2, write replace -- value cells disclosed by class
  CONTROL ctrl live, ctrl devsig sh4, ctrl devsig maple, ctrl zlive
The nine READ sessions: val_a, val_b, other read, survive, initial, four, all ones, double, replace.

PREDICTIONS (score / 16; the failing rows):
  BASE         16/16  CONTROL=OK
  HEAD          5/16  every read session dies on its first DMAADDR read: val_a, val_b, marker survive, exit status
                      (exit1), initial zero, read four, read all ones, double read 1, double read 2, write replace FAIL;
                      read silent 8/9 (every read session but `other read' prints the TODO) FAIL.  `other read' PASSES
                      (it reads RESET2, never DMAADDR).  Controls OK.  11 failing.
  M_KEEPFATAL  15/16  read silent ALONE (8/9)
  M_REWORD     15/16  read silent ALONE (8/9) -- the reworded text still names `dreamcast_maple'
  M_LATCHED    15/16  read silent ALONE (8/9) -- one print per process, and each session is a process
  M_EXITONLY    6/16  as HEAD but read silent PASSES (0/9: nothing printed) -- 10 failing
  M_RET0        8/16  the load is skipped and every destination keeps POISON: val_a, val_b, initial zero, read four,
                      read all ones, double read 1, double read 2, write replace FAIL (8); other read, marker, exit
                      status and read silent pass (the failed-access message is debug(), invisible here -- a
                      PREDICTION on verbosity, and if it is wrong read silent reds too: 7/16)
  M_DECLINE     9/16  odata stays 0: val_a, val_b, read four, read all ones, double 1, double 2, write replace FAIL (7);
                      initial zero PASSES (0 == 0)
  M_HOIST      15/16  other read ALONE (RESET2 answers 0x8c012345)
  M_READCLEAR  15/16  double read 2 ALONE (0)
  M_EQ4        15/16  read four ALONE (that session dies: absent)
  M_BIT30      15/16  read all ones ALONE -- 0x40000000 is set by no other value (0x8c012345, 0x0c00001f, 4, 0x13579bdf)
  M_ZEROEXIT   15/16  initial zero ALONE
  M_MASKLOW     9/16  val_a, val_b, read four, read all ones, double 1, double 2, write replace FAIL (7); initial zero
                      passes (0 & ~0x1f == 0)

DISCRIMINATING CLAIMS: each of M_HOIST, M_READCLEAR, M_EQ4, M_BIT30, M_ZEROEXIT has exactly ONE killer, and it is the
row the ruling assigned; the three announce legs die on `read silent' alone.

CHECKS.  SIBLING PARITY -- MAPLE_ENABLE's read (odata = d->enable, quiet) is the model the fix follows; no other arm
edited.  CLAIM -> ROW -- the #528 comment claims "no diagnostic and no exit" -> read silent, marker survive, exit
status; "answered like MAPLE_ENABLE's read" -> the value rows; the CONTRACT's NO-ROW sentence covers the post-DMA
value.  GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the body reads d->dmaaddr only, written by the write arm and maple_do_dma_xfer's
tail; no state where they disagree is reachable without DMA (deferred, by name, to mapledmaadvance).  CHANNEL -- each
value row reads a poisoned register, so a skipped or zeroed load reds it; read silent reads the transcript, which
varies under any announce; other read reads RESET2, which varies only under a hoist.
